  "id": "COMPOUND:32713 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that the compound 3beta-(alpha-L-rhamnopyranosyloxy)-1beta,5beta,11alpha,14beta,19beta-pentahydroxy-5beta-card-20(22)-enolide may interact with DNA polymerase iota through multiple indirect pathways. The compound is identified as a target of Bezerramycin B and (1R,6S,7R)-3,7-Dimethyl-7-(4-methyl-3-penten-1-yl)bicyclo(4.1.0)hept-2-ene, both of which are known to target DNA polymerase iota. Additionally, the compound is linked to Thrombopoietin, which in turn is a target of another compound that also targets DNA polymerase iota. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may exert its effect on DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving signaling pathways or enzymatic activities. The evidence is consistent with the compound acting as a modulator or inhibitor of DNA polymerase iota, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
